cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "QMBL - the Quantum Many-Body Leaderboard"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it. Individual energies should cite the primary paper named on the row."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Zerweck
    given-names: Tristan
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-14"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22753734
repository-code: "https://github.com/tzerweck/quantum-many-body-leaderboard"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22753734
    description: "Concept DOI - always resolves to the latest release"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22753735
    description: "v0.1.0 snapshot: 205 instances, 675 rows, 182 records"
abstract: >-
  A live record of the best published variational ground-state energies for lattice
  Hamiltonians, ranked by energy, with an explicit bound_type on every row so that
  variational, projected, extrapolated and exact results are never mixed. Each row
  cites the primary paper that produced the number. The starting set of references was
  bootstrapped from the VarBench compilation (Wu et al., Science 386, 296 (2024)),
  Apache-2.0, which is credited as a source of references, not as a parent work.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Variational Benchmarks for Quantum Many-Body Problems"
    doi: 10.1126/science.adg9774
    year: 2024
